✔ root race, real runtime: close() while the exit grant is in flight withdraws the late circuit; no circuit, grant, child or timer survives (130.856024ms)
✔ close() during a slow tunnel handshake ends the startup at once: no exit grant is ever asked, nothing lingers (331.854085ms)
✔ a ban during BACKGROUND reconcile: the live circuit is withdrawn first, the one still being built is withdrawn when it answers (177.258336ms)
✔ delayed failure: the exit REFUSES the grant it was holding while the host stopped: nothing to withdraw, no strike, clean stop (54.632144ms)
✔ delayed failure AFTER a grant (the exit granted other names): the runtime withdraws that grant before its tunnel ends (52.064118ms)
✔ the privacy agent switch: a ban DURING the first startup stops it at once; the admin's re-admit starts a fresh transport that serves (1153.17461ms)
✔ the privacy agent switch: a ban during a BACKGROUND round of a serving transport withdraws everything; app circuits are untouched (1191.672339ms)
✔ agent stop during a startup: close() resolves only after the cancelled startup ended; a later judge() starts nothing (464.640494ms)
✔ root probe shape (a runtime that ignores the stop): the late circuit is withdrawn and closed, never inserted; no timer (0.928531ms)
✔ a startup that outlives the stop's settle bound: close() resolves at the bound; the late circuit is still withdrawn when it answers (201.189881ms)
